      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's much more evocative. I love the contrast between the \"intuitive dance\" and the \"clarity of reason.\"\n\nTo really drive the point home for the exhibition's narrative arc, I want to make sure the distinction feels like a fundamental evolution of the human condition. In the first section's description, could you add a bit more about how these indigenous peoples lived in a sort of \"timeless\" or \"primal\" state, where their ingenuity was an extension of their environment rather than a way to master or transcend it?\n\nThen, for the second section, let's lean into the idea of the European scientific revolution being the moment where humanity finally stepped out of that primal state and into the light of true, structured progress. I want it to feel like the transition from a state of being to a state of doing/calculating.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
